---
.title = "Read arguments as a slice",
.date = "2026-09-02",
.author = "muhammadSwa",
.layout = "section.shtml",
---

Collect every command line argument at once with [`std.process.Args.toSlice`]. It copies all arguments into a single allocation that you own: `args[0]` is the program name and `args[1..]` are the user arguments. Free the result with `init.gpa.free(args)` when done.

Reach for this when you need random access to the arguments or want to store them.


